<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Famine (Ireland)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1845">1845</a>–<a href="/years/1852">1852</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Irish Famine, Irish Potato Famine</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Famine was a period of mass starvation and disease in Ireland from 1845 to 1852, caused by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potato">potato</a> blight that destroyed the staple crop of the rural poor. Worsened by British government policy, evictions and continued food exports, it killed about a million people and drove a million or more to emigrate, reducing Ireland's population by about a quarter.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-famine-ireland.jpg" alt="Great Famine (Ireland)" width="320" height="442" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Mahony · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skibbereen_by_James_Mahony,_1847.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Great Famine</b> of 1845–1852, caused by potato blight and worsened by government policy and evictions, killed about a million people and drove another million to emigrate; Ireland’s population fell from about 8.2 million in 1841 to 4.4 million in 1911.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-ireland">United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
